# Record Architecture Decisions

We will record architectural decisions made on this project as Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) under `docs/adr/`, following the lightweight format described by `grill-with-docs`.

An ADR is created when all three are true: the decision is hard to reverse, would surprise a future reader without context, and was the result of a real trade-off between alternatives. Routine choices and easily-reversible decisions are not recorded — they live in code and commit history.

ADE's Research phase (R4 Refine) invokes `grill-with-docs`, which surfaces ADR-worthy decisions during spec creation and writes them here. The format is intentionally minimal — a title plus one to three sentences capturing context, decision, and rationale.
